From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:57:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virgl: answer the reset query a robust context owes

Mesa's EGL advertises EGL_EXT_create_context_robustness, and with it
EXT_query_reset_notification_strategy, only when the screen sets
`device_reset_status_query`. The virgl driver never set it, so
`eglCreateContext` refused every robust context with EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE and
KHR-NoContext.gl43.robust_buffer_access_behavior.vertex_buffer_objects and
KHR-NoContext.gl45.robustness.no_reset_notification failed on a guest running
the virgl Gallium driver. Guest Zink sets the cap, which is why the same cases
passed on the stack that ran the CTS through it.

The host already reports whether it gave this context robust buffer access,
through VIRGL_CAP_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS, so the cap follows that bit and needs
no protocol change. Answering the query it then owes is exact rather than
approximate: a renderer that loses its device loses the command stream this
context lives in, so a context still alive to be asked has not observed a
reset, and PIPE_NO_RESET is the whole truth a live guest context can report.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_context.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c  |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_context.c
index bfc98350e03acf420d469f687411db8403e85ca1..fb8c4aede1d83bafc4b5523713e41b56add16edc 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_context.c
@@ -1594,6 +1594,15 @@ virgl_emit_string_marker(struct pipe_context *ctx, const char *message,  int len
     virgl_encode_emit_string_marker(vctx, message, len);
 }
 
+static enum pipe_reset_status
+virgl_get_device_reset_status(UNUSED struct pipe_context *ctx)
+{
+   /* A renderer that loses its device takes this context's command stream
+    * with it, so a context that is still alive to be asked has not seen a
+    * reset. */
+   return PIPE_NO_RESET;
+}
+
 static void
 virgl_context_destroy( struct pipe_context *ctx )
 {
@@ -1811,6 +1820,9 @@ struct pipe_context *virgl_context_create(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
    vctx->base.memory_barrier = virgl_memory_barrier;
    vctx->base.emit_string_marker = virgl_emit_string_marker;
 
+   if (rs->caps.caps.v2.capability_bits & VIRGL_CAP_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS)
+      vctx->base.get_device_reset_status = virgl_get_device_reset_status;
+
    vctx->base.create_video_codec = virgl_video_create_codec;
    vctx->base.create_video_buffer = virgl_video_create_buffer;
 
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
index 66b3d3d6368d7f58dc23ba61fa716baae04878f1..66011893bc079509c08e55dfd2d63d633357f592 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
@@ -416,6 +416,10 @@ virgl_init_screen_caps(struct virgl_screen *vscreen)
       vscreen->caps.caps.v2.capability_bits & VIRGL_CAP_FB_NO_ATTACH;
    caps->robust_buffer_access_behavior =
       vscreen->caps.caps.v2.capability_bits & VIRGL_CAP_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS;
+   /* The host reports a robust context through the same bit, and a guest
+    * context can always answer the reset query it then owes the caller. */
+   caps->device_reset_status_query =
+      vscreen->caps.caps.v2.capability_bits & VIRGL_CAP_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS;
    caps->fbfetch =
       (vscreen->caps.caps.v2.capability_bits & VIRGL_CAP_TGSI_FBFETCH) ? 1 : 0;
    caps->blend_equation_advanced =
